This repository is a release snapshot of a Lean 4 formalization of Theorem 1 of the PSI paper
"Entanglement Breaking after 2(d-1) PPT Maps". The Lean files under PPTCompositionBound/ are taken
from PSI's development repository, with the Lean module-system header added, one declaration made
private as the module system requires, and minor comment edits; the axiom check
PPTCompositionBound/Audit/FinalCheck.lean was added for this release.

Comparator checks that the theorems proved in
Solution.lean are exactly the statements in Challenge.lean, using only the three standard axioms,
and the proofs are replayed by Lean's kernel and by independent kernels.

Provenance and use of AI. This result was released by Physical Superintelligence (PSI). The
mathematics was developed by PSI researchers working with AI models (OpenAI's GPT-5.6-Sol, GPT-5.6
Pro and GPT-6-Astra and Anthropic's Claude Opus 5) in automated research workflows at PSI. The Lean
formalization was written by AI agents (Anthropic's Claude Opus 5.5 in Claude Code, and OpenAI's GPT-6-Astra in Codex) under PSI's direction. David
Turturean and Ning Bao are responsible for the correctness of the paper. The paper's AI disclosure
has the details; formalization.yaml records which agent did which part.

